  "summary_en": "Adra's fourth Strategic Research, Innovation and Deployment Agenda sets out an AI, data and robotics vision for 2030 and recommendations for Horizon Europe 2025-27. It is organised as six \"Big Tickets\", including next-generation robots with embodied intelligence and tools for compliance. It calls for regulatory sandboxes, standardisation, test facilities and adaptable regulation to support trustworthy, competitive European innovation.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Six Big Tickets for 2025-27, including next-generation robots with embodied intelligence (Big Ticket 4) and research tools for compliance (Big Ticket 6)",
   "Proposes a European Robotics Catalyst that uses market pull, public procurement and de-risked venture capital for robotics start-ups",
   "Calls for regulatory sandboxes, testing and experimentation facilities, and European standards for robot modularity, certification and validation",
   "Advocates adaptable regulation with sunset or revision clauses, and fast regulator guidance on complying with the AI Act, Machinery, Cyber Resilience and Data Acts",
   "Says physical and non-physical human-robot interaction should follow safety and process regulation"
  ],
